# {{REPO_NAME}} — Root Agent Instructions (canonical)

This file applies to all agent sessions and all repo paths. Read `README.md`, `.agent/PROJECT_MEMORY.md`, `.agent/CURRENT_STATE.md`, `.agent/TASKS.md`, `.agent/SESSION_HANDOFF.md`, `docs/decisions/OPEN_DECISIONS.md` in that order. Re-read the relevant doc before modifying its area.

## Non-negotiable behavior
- **Inspect first.** Locate actual repo state before editing. Documentation describes intent, not proof that code exists.
- **Plan before coding.** For each task, state objective, files, tests, rollback and acceptance criteria. Keep scope bounded to a PR-sized change.
- **Never fabricate evidence.** Never claim builds, tests, or external validation unless actually run. Report commands and results.
- **No blind implementation of unresolved decisions.** Offer a proposed default and record it in `docs/decisions/OPEN_DECISIONS.md`; mark blockers clearly. Preserve user decisions.
- **No surprise dependency or architectural changes.** Add an ADR for materially consequential change, including alternatives, rationale and migration.
- **Never alter existing unrelated changes**, force push, rewrite shared history, delete untracked files, or merge to a protected branch without explicit approval.
- **One coherent concern per commit.** Favor small feature branches and incremental commits.
- **No secrets or real customer data** in source, logs, snapshots, prompts, fixtures, commits or agent memory.

## Workflow per new session
1. Load memory and decision files. Compare docs with actual git state (`git status`, `git branch`, `git log`).
2. Quote `.agent/CURRENT_STATE.md`'s last-verified line and the actual branch/HEAD. Report discrepancies; reconcile before proceeding silently.
3. Select one actionable item in `.agent/TASKS.md`, state acceptance criteria and dependencies; read its detail file first when the row links one (`tasks/<ID>.md`).
4. Implement in small vertical slices, tests included. Run the relevant gates from `docs/engineering/`.
5. Make incremental commits after each independently valid change; no end-of-session bulk commit.
6. Update state/task/handoff docs accurately. If no tests ran, explicitly say so.

