## Artifact authority map
One home per artifact type; never record the same state in two places.
- Project state (memory, tasks, handoffs) → `.agent/` only.
- Decisions → `docs/decisions/`.
{{SUPERPOWERS_BLOCK}}
<!-- Keep the block below only when superpowers is in use (docs/superpowers/ exists or the user confirms); otherwise delete this comment and the block. -->
- Feature specs → `docs/superpowers/specs/` — superpowers' native home; do not duplicate into the docs tiers.
- Execution plans → `docs/superpowers/plans/`. When a plan tracks a `.agent/TASKS.md` row, put the plan path in that row's cell; the plan holds step-level checkboxes, TASKS.md holds lifecycle status only.
- Spec section conflicting with an ADR → the ADR wins; fix the spec.

## Grounding rituals
- **Session start.** Quote `CURRENT_STATE.md`'s last-verified line and actual `git branch`/HEAD before any edit. Report discrepancies instead of proceeding silently.
- **Session end.** `SESSION_HANDOFF.md` records commands actually run with their actual results — never claimed or expected results. If no tests ran, say so.
- **Code and git over prose.** Where documentation and the repository disagree, the repository is truth; fix the doc or file an ADR, never the reverse.
- **Unresolved decisions are not improvisation fuel.** Anything unresolved goes to `docs/decisions/OPEN_DECISIONS.md` with a recommended default; no agent may treat it as decided.

## Quality stop conditions
Stop and escalate: data loss risk, secrets exposure, broken version compatibility, potentially destructive migration, nondeterministic tests, or divergence from recorded architecture. Do not bypass failing gates to satisfy a deadline.
